  "body": "The Wire Contour operation supports open runs with a stated kerf side (#1109). The native Agie post in #2951 accepts only a closed punch.\n\nPost a straight open cut with an explicit left or right side and a supported resident process. Require both wire endpoints to clear opposite faces of the stock. Check the wire, machine travel and hold of the released piece.\n\nA synthetic offline controller job showed why the second start point matters. With both native start points at the entry, the wire made an extra cutting move across the stock after each pass. With a separate exit outside the opposite stock face, all four passes followed their intended offsets. The rough pass releases the piece before the trims start.\n\nVerify the normal CAMCraft operation on both sides. Check the return moves and their compensation against the controller plot. Refuse a missing exit, unsupported holding or an unsafe path before creating the job directory.\n\nSuggested labels are P6, effort:high, area:post, enhancement and source:agent.\n",
